        "Abstract": "In recent years, tremendous effort has been put into the research and development of task-oriented dialogue agents; yet, it has been mainly focused on only a handful of popular languages, hindering the adoption of dialogue technology around the globe. Collecting dialogue data from scratch for a new language is ideal but prohibitively expensive and time-consuming, leading to the current lack of reliable multilingual dialogue benchmarks."
